# A small history of Linux
It is well known because of the Free and Open source speciality. 
Earlier the well known Os were Unix & Minix - It had it's own configurations and restrictions for different use cases.
Linus Torvalds - developed an OS which is customized to his own use cases as a hobby inspired from Unix and Minix. Later it was provided to public.
Linux is actually a kernel not an operating system (the bridge between the hardware and the os)

Richard Stallman (American Software Programmer and Activist), while working in MIT encountered some software issues while troubleshooting a printer at lab, so he realized the need of something which can be tweaked as per the need,
which led to GNU (GNU's not Unix), - control over technology
Free doesn't mean cashless, it's freedom (GNU introduced GPL - General Public License, which proposed 4 freedoms)
1. Freedom to use as you wish
2. Freedom to understand the working (access to source code)
3. Freedom to redistribute to anyone
4. Freedom to customize as per the need and distribute with the changes
Debian, ArchLinux, fedora - are some foundational distributions
from Debian -> Ubuntu, Kali, Parrot OS
from Archlinux -> Steam OS
from Fedora -> Redhat 
etc.

